  "title": "The Pocket-Sized Home",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "silent emotional stories",
  "premise": "A traveler wants to unpack in a bare temporary room, but the oversized suitcase makes every object feel out of place. They find one small familiar drawing in a side pocket, tape it beside the bed, and gradually arrange the room around that single recognizable corner.",
  "hook": "Start with one familiar corner.",
  "visible_action": "Suitcase opens over empty floor; objects hover indecisively; a small drawing is placed; lamp, cup, and blanket settle nearby.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "One familiar detail can be a starting point for a new space.",
  "gate": "Keep the circumstances of temporary housing unspecified; no claim that decoration resolves displacement or hardship.",
  "evidence_class": "fictional_demonstration",
